      {
        "id": 95294,
        "name": "JimmytheRat",
        "username": "JimmytheRat",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/c37758/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-16T00:17:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm actually kinda wary about using Imbued Fire against the Ennead.&nbsp; While it boosts everyone's damage and gets rid of Shu's immunity, a third of the Ennead's deck deals fire damage to all hero targets, and Atum and Nephthys get a lot worse.&nbsp; It's much more of a gamble against them than against other villains.&nbsp; (Adaptive Plating Subroutine has a nasty habit of showing up 1-2 turns after Imbued Fire comes out, though...)</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
